            "review_title": "Review at An Tuong Cafe",
            "review_text": "DirtyPierreOnTour\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12578 contributions\n0\nWell worth the long ride out from HCMC\nJun 2016 • Solo\nAn Tuong Cafe is in a beautiful garden setting at least an hours motorbike ride from HCMC. Even longer if travelling in a taxi.\nVery comprehensive Western menu.\nTheir ham cheese and tomato toasted sandwich was excellent. Thick pieces of European style ham with cheese and salad and toasted correctly which is a rarity in Vietnam. Mostly it's warm bread you get, but this was different, crunchy brown toast.\nI will be back with friends to try other items on the menu. \nI was a little disappointed that all the lovely soups I wanted to try were not available. Maybe next time they will be on the menu. \nTwo very friendly puppies periodically came to visit my table for a pat. Very cute. \nBecause of the length of time it takes to visit I would only come for lunch if staying in HCMC as I would never travel on that road in the dark because of the truck traffic. But if you are staying in the Binh Duong area then it would be an ideal place for dinner. Their menu prices were reasonable too. \nStaff are friendly and wear nicely designed uniforms. \nAll round lovely atmosphere.\nI look forward to my next visit.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 28, 2016",
